{
  "file": "module4",
  "page": 165,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        66.76272583007812,
        216.29168701171875,
        82.6147232055664
      ],
      "text": "Justification and evidence",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        89.82263946533203,
        374.89404296875,
        104.26564025878906
      ],
      "text": "The recommendation in this section addresses one PICO question:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.47807312011719,
        110.25061798095703,
        515.9675903320312,
        125.91461944580078
      ],
      "text": "(DR-TB, 2011): In patients with HIV infection and drug-resistant TB receiving  PICO question",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.86609649658203,
        123.45063018798828,
        516.0079345703125,
        139.11463928222656
      ],
      "text": "antiretroviral therapy, is the use of drugs with overlapping and potentially additive toxicities,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.86609649658203,
        136.65065002441406,
        475.1916809082031,
        152.3146514892578
      ],
      "text": "compared with their avoidance, more or less likely to lead to cure or other outcomes? 59",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        158.35450744628906,
        527.2767333984375,
        174.07350158691406
      ],
      "text": "(123–132) Evidence was reviewed from 10 studies  , to assess patient treatment outcomes when ART and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.955760955810547,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        172.8303985595703,
        527.4200439453125,
        187.2733917236328
      ],
      "text": "second-line antituberculosis drugs were used together. None of the data were from RCTs. IPD were",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        186.03053283691406,
        527.4332885742188,
        200.47352600097656
      ],
      "text": "available for 217 patients with DR-TB, of whom 127 received ART. The level of evidence in individual",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.2305450439453,
        331.11517333984375,
        213.6735382080078
      ],
      "text": "observational studies varied from low to very low quality.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.04769897460938,
        188.62208557128906,
        242.89968872070312
      ],
      "text": "Summary of findings",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        250.1077423095703,
        527.1878662109375,
        264.5507507324219
      ],
      "text": "The pooled IPD from longitudinal cohort studies showed a lower risk of death and a higher likelihood",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.98819351196289,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        263.3076171875,
        527.44873046875,
        277.7506408691406
      ],
      "text": "of cure, and resolution of TB signs and symptoms in patients using ART, compared with those not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        276.50762939453125,
        527.5742797851562,
        290.9506530761719
      ],
      "text": "using ART (low-quality evidence). There is very low certainty evidence for other outcomes that",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        289.70758056640625,
        524.3762817382812,
        304.1506042480469
      ],
      "text": "were considered critical or important for decision-making (e.g. severe adverse effects from second-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        302.9075927734375,
        527.390380859375,
        317.3506164550781
      ],
      "text": "line drugs for DR-TB, occurrence of sputum smear or culture conversion, interactions of ART with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        316.10772705078125,
        527.5914306640625,
        330.5507507324219
      ],
      "text": "antituberculosis drugs and default from treatment). Available data did not allow assessment for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        329.3076171875,
        527.425537109375,
        343.7506408691406
      ],
      "text": "several other outcomes of interest; namely, avoiding the acquisition of additional drug resistance,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        342.5075988769531,
        527.0967407226562,
        356.95062255859375
      ],
      "text": "preventing TB transmission, sustaining relapse-free cure, establishing the optimal duration of MDR-TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.975974082946777,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        355.7076110839844,
        527.5350952148438,
        370.150634765625
      ],
      "text": "treatment, avoiding unnecessary MDR-TB treatment, reducing costs and improving population access",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.970861434936523,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        368.9075927734375,
        161.69639587402344,
        383.3506164550781
      ],
      "text": "to appropriate care.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        396.72491455078125,
        116.5405044555664,
        412.576904296875
      ],
      "text": "Benefits",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        419.7848205566406,
        527.3993530273438,
        434.22784423828125
      ],
      "text": "The strong recommendation for the use of ART is based in part on indirect evidence from its use",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        432.98480224609375,
        527.4520874023438,
        447.4278259277344
      ],
      "text": "in any patient with active TB, which shows large beneficial effects and a very high mortality when",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        444.9088134765625,
        527.5244750976562,
        460.6278381347656
      ],
      "text": "(133) ART is not employed   particularly in highly immunocompromised patients (CD4 cell count",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        458.1087951660156,
        527.2796020507812,
        473.82781982421875
      ],
      "text": "(134, 135) <50 cells/mm )  . In the absence of other data specific to patients with DR-TB receiving  3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        472.5848083496094,
        527.4378051757812,
        487.02783203125
      ],
      "text": "second-line antituberculosis medication, the decision on when to start ART should be no different",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        485.7848205566406,
        527.4334716796875,
        500.22784423828125
      ],
      "text": "from the approach to a patient living with HIV with drug-susceptible TB. ART should thus be initiated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        498.98480224609375,
        527.395751953125,
        513.4277954101562
      ],
      "text": "regardless of CD4 cell count and as soon as antituberculosis treatment is tolerated, ideally as early as",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        510.9088134765625,
        527.42138671875,
        526.6278076171875
      ],
      "text": "(133, 136) 2 weeks and no later than 8 weeks after initiation of antituberculosis treatment  . However,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        525.384765625,
        527.4190673828125,
        539.8277587890625
      ],
      "text": "for TB patients living with HIV with profound immunosuppression (e.g. CD4 counts <50 cells/mm ),  3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        537.308837890625,
        430.3622741699219,
        553.02783203125
      ],
      "text": "(110) they should receive ART within the first 2 weeks of initiating TB treatment  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        566.4019775390625,
        99.6792984008789,
        582.2540283203125
      ],
      "text": "Risks",
      "font": "SegoeUI-BoldItalic",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        589.4620361328125,
        527.5850830078125,
        603.905029296875
      ],
      "text": "The successful implementation of this recommendation will depend on the availability of more",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        602.6619873046875,
        527.3850708007812,
        617.10498046875
      ],
      "text": "providers trained specifically in the care of HIV and DR-TB, and drug–drug interactions. A substantial",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        615.8619384765625,
        527.4234008789062,
        630.304931640625
      ],
      "text": "increase in the availability of and patient’s access to treatment, and additional support for ensuring",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        629.0618896484375,
        527.4202880859375,
        643.5048828125
      ],
      "text": "adherence would probably be needed. The need for increased integration of HIV and TB care for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        642.2620239257812,
        527.4057006835938,
        656.7050170898438
      ],
      "text": "effective patient management, prompt evaluation of adverse events and case-holding throughout",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        673.0717163085938,
        526.4263916015625,
        686.7756958007812
      ],
      "text": "The outcomes considered for this question comprised: 1. Cure (treatment failure), 2. Prompt initiation of appropriate treatment,  59",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        685.8717041015625,
        526.7710571289062,
        696.3756713867188
      ],
      "text": "3. Avoiding the acquisition or amplification of drug resistance, 4. Survival (death from TB), 5. Staying disease-free after treatment;",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        695.4717407226562,
        526.5751342773438,
        705.9757080078125
      ],
      "text": "sustaining a cure (relapse), 6. Case-holding so the TB patient remains adherent to treatment (default or treatment interruption due to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        705.0717163085938,
        526.7238159179688,
        715.57568359375
      ],
      "text": "non-adherence), 7. Population coverage or access to appropriate treatment of DR-TB, 8. Smear or culture conversion during treatment,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 7.992546558380127,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        714.6716918945312,
        526.60302734375,
        725.1756591796875
      ],
      "text": "9. Accelerated detection of drug resistance, 10. Avoidance of unnecessary MDR-TB treatment, 11. Population coverage or access to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        724.271728515625,
        526.6046752929688,
        734.7756958007812
      ],
      "text": "diagnosis of DR-TB, 12. Prevention or interruption of transmission of DR-TB to other people, including other patients and health care",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        733.8717041015625,
        526.5975952148438,
        744.3756713867188
      ],
      "text": "workers, 13. Shortest possible duration of treatment, 14. Avoiding toxicity and adverse reactions from antituberculosis drugs, 15. Cost",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        743.4717407226562,
        526.6039428710938,
        753.9757080078125
      ],
      "text": "to the patient, including direct medical costs and other costs such as transportation and lost wages due to disability, 16. Resolution of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        753.0717163085938,
        526.5886840820312,
        763.57568359375
      ],
      "text": "TB signs and symptoms; ability to resume usual life activities, 17. Interaction of antituberculosis drugs with non-TB medications, and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        762.6716918945312,
        210.76531982421875,
        773.1756591796875
      ],
      "text": "18. Cost to the TB control programme.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        330.23760986328125,
        801.0170288085938,
        556.099609375,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "Chapter 2 Drug-resistant TB treatment: Recommendations  151",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}